====== COMMIT demo: changes are visible after COMMIT ======

DROP TABLE
CREATE TABLE
BEGIN
INSERT 0 1
INSERT 0 1
COMMIT
After COMMIT, rows visible to all sessions:
 id |      note       |          created_at           
----+-----------------+-------------------------------
  1 | committed row 1 | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.754482+01
  2 | committed row 2 | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.754482+01
(2 rows)


====== ROLLBACK demo: changes discarded after ROLLBACK ======

BEGIN
INSERT 0 1
INSERT 0 1
Inside the transaction, we can see them:
 rows_inside_txn 
-----------------
               4
(1 row)

ROLLBACK
After ROLLBACK, the inserted rows are gone:
 rows_after_rollback 
---------------------
                   2
(1 row)


====== SAVEPOINT demo: partial rollback inside a transaction ======

BEGIN
INSERT 0 1
SAVEPOINT
INSERT 0 1
ROLLBACK
INSERT 0 1
COMMIT
After COMMIT, only the two non-rolled-back rows are visible:
 id |      note       |          created_at           
----+-----------------+-------------------------------
  1 | committed row 1 | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.754482+01
  2 | committed row 2 | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.754482+01
  5 | will survive    | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.758255+01
  7 | also survives   | 2026-11-12 14:57:58.758255+01
(4 rows)


====== TRIGGER-driven rollback: a payment insert that violates a CHECK =====
       is automatically rolled back when the outer block fails.

DROP TABLE
CREATE TABLE
BEGIN
INSERT 0 1
ROLLBACK
After ROLLBACK, the demo table is empty (the 5000 row was undone together with the 0 row):
 rows_in_p3_payment_demo 
-------------------------
                       0
(1 row)

